{{Illusionnotes
| name = Necromastery
| desc = Nevermore's created {{M|illusions}} starts with 0 stacks, and can gain stacks themselves.<br><br>Does not benefit from the flat {{M|bonus attack damage}} component.
}}
{{Breaknotes
| name = Necromastery
| desc = Disables the buff stack gain.<br><br>However, existing stacks are not removed.
}}


{{Illusionnotes
| name = Necromastery
| desc = Nevermore's created {{M|illusions}} starts with 0 stacks, and can gain stacks themselves.<br><br>Does not benefit from the flat {{M|bonus attack damage}} component.
}}
{{Breaknotes
| name = Necromastery
| desc = Disables the buff stack gain.<br><br>However, existing stacks are not removed.
}}

 * {{Symbol|Modifier|Stack}}
** Grants flat {{M|bonus attack damage}} stack from killing any units, regardless of the ability visual effects, including from {{M|deny|text=denies}}.
*** Considers {{M|clones}} and the {{H|Spirit Bear}} as heroes, {{M|illusions}} and other {{M|creep-heroes}} as creeps.
** Does not grant stacks from killing the following units:
*** Allied {{I|Observer Ward|text=Observer Wards}} and {{I|Sentry Ward|text=Sentry Wards}} {{M|denies}}.
*** {{M|Buildings}}
*** {{M|The Double}}.
*** {{M|Illusions}}
*** {{M|Items}}
*** {{M|Runes}}
*** {{M|Ward-type units}}.
** {{Symbol|Death}}
*** The current number of stacks is rounded down upon [[death]] and is defined as:
**** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|[[Wikipedia:Floor and ceiling functions|⌊]] {{#var:Necromastery value2}} × f(Stack) [[Wikipedia:Floor and ceiling functions|⌋]]}}
***** Hence, Nevermore can never lose all stacks.
***** Does not lose stacks with {{M|reincarnation}} sources.

* {{cf|expr}}
** Flat {{M|bonus attack damage}}: {{Code|({{#var:Necromastery value4}} + {{#var:Necromastery basic1}} × SelfLvl / {{#var:Necromastery type2 value1}}) × f(Stack)}}

